@@ -115,6 +115,8 @@ Session rows accept Tab focus and open with unmodified Enter or Space; Tab also
 
 Client callers can pass `prompt`, `whenDraftExists`, and `clearPreviousDraft` in the second argument to `uiWorkspace.startSession`. A prompt is plain text; structured drafts are handled internally during restoration and Workspace transfer. An empty draft adopts the prompt. When the target already has text or attachments, `whenDraftExists: 'keep'` (the default) preserves them, `'replace'` replaces only the target Session's text and inline references with the prompt or clears them without one, and `'append'` adds the prompt as new paragraphs after the existing text; attachments stay in every case. `clearPreviousDraft: true` acts as `'replace'` only when `whenDraftExists` is omitted. Option values are captured before asynchronous creation and applied to the exact retained binding before navigation commits. Superseded navigation does not write content; a submission-blocked input refuses preparation and keeps the previous selection. Calls with or without options open the blank Session chosen as described above, so New Session returns to its unsent draft. The [draft initialization decision](../../../.agents/notes/implemented/architecture/2026-09-30-structured-draft-initialization.md) describes the input owner's data flow.
 
+The root-scoped `sidebar.workspaces.delete` slot receives the selected Workspace ID, title, and close callback. A plugin can supply its own confirmation. An empty slot renders the built-in Workspace removal dialog.
+
 ### The directory-flow hole
 
 Each registration declares a **directory-flow child hole** (`single` kind: `conversation.hero.workspace.directoryFlow` / `sidebar.workspaces.directoryFlow`), and the `workspace.picker` Factory declares `workspace.picker.directoryFlow`; the composed picker package's client half fills all three with its picking interaction — the `-native` backend's renderless OS-chooser driver, an in-app browsing dialog under a `-browse` composition. The flat **Add workspace...** action renders only while the surface's hole is occupied; an empty hole means the composition has no picking affordance. The sidebar Add workspace action preserves an existing blank Session and its draft. This package owns the trigger and the adoption: the occupant reports one picked path per open through the hole's owner conversation (`open`/`busy`/`onPicked`/`onCancel`/`onError`), and the owner adopts it through the object layer, selecting the committed Workspace only after its list projection has refreshed.
